{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Q1WS65ZdBicj61Qhir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] The new subsection covers URL schemes, `<script>` and `<style>` contexts, `raw`, invalid attribute names, and the void element rule.\n[x] `npm run toc` has been run and the table of contents lists the subsection.\n[x] The section contains no em dashes and no arrow characters.\n\nI added a \"What escaping does not cover\" subsection to `README.md`, under `microtags/htm`, right after the existing paragraphs on escaping, void elements and custom elements. It covers five things:\n\n1. **URL schemes:** attribute escaping does not stop a `javascript:` URL in attributes like `href`, `src` or `action`. Authors need to check the scheme themselves, for example allowing only `http:`, `https:` and `mailto:`.\n2. **`<script>` and `<style>`:** HTML escaping is the wrong encoding inside these, so user data should not go there. To pass data to a script, it points to the JSON script with `<` escaped that the hydration example already uses.\n3. **`raw`:** it skips escaping by design, so it should only ever get trusted markup.\n4. **Attribute names:** it gives the naming rule. Names that break it are skipped without an error on the server, in the browser and on a component's host tag. I checked this against the actual checks in `src/htm.ts`, `src/htm.browser.ts` and `src/builders.ts`.\n5. **Void elements:** a void element with children throws, so write the self-closing form.\n\nRunning `npm run toc` added the new entry. It also removed eight old entries under \"Hydration\" that pointed to headings no longer in the README. That is correct regeneration, but it does show up in the diff.\n\nThere are no tests, because the rules say not to test docs. As the final check, `npm test` passed 413/413. Everything is committed except `.nightralph/notes.md`, which the instructions say to leave uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":279,"cache_read_input_tokens":58026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":279},"output_tokens":612,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6ac160b-fa41-4795-9657-89e14eb8e6d5","uuid":"8d109559-c919-4c0b-a61e-3d408cdd5633","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:32:53.596Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Q1WAUBZBtJtSu8CVq1"}
